; spec_accept_phantom_arg_read_template_reader.ll — ACCEPT with the hand-inlined twin's
; stream (bd test_C_libtooling-tzfa; bd vsfp Rule-13 r2B F-WB-1 `k19`, IR-only spelling).
;
; `@h`'s read of `a` is BRANCH-ONLY (an empty diamond, so the drop cannot predict the dead
; slot); the clone's flatten kills it and the specializer records slot 0 dead. The phantom
; operand is `p = q * 3`, a template rail the phase oracle `(p ^ q) == 10` also reads. Round
; 2 ACCEPTED because `p` "had another reader" and left `h(p, m)` in place: the spine saw two
; consumers of `p`'s rail and never uncomputed it — `q` fully dephased (a Rule-8 wrong
; unitary; round 1 declined). Round 3 neutralises the slot (`h(0, m)`), so the spine sees the
; twin's consumer set: `cq_template_mul_i32_hl_unc` + `cqrt_free` of `p` before the second
; Ry. Remove the neutralisation (mutant N1) and this file goes red.
; ⚠ ROUND 3 (bd tzfa; Rule-13 r2B F-WB-1). A slot the specializer RECORDED dead is now
; NEUTRALISED after `specialize()` (`resolvePhantomCloneArgReads`: the argument becomes `0`,
; the drop's rewrite), so the uncompute spine, M-C, M-A and stage 2b see the hand-inlined
; twin's consumer set. Round 2 instead ACCEPTED a phantom read whose operand had another
; reader and left the read in place — one consumer too many for the spine.
;
; Caller (r2B `k19`): `int q = m & 7; cq_theta(&q, .5); int p = q * 3; int r = h(p, m); int u = p ^ q;
;   if (u == 10) cq_phi(3.14159); cq_theta(&q, .7); return r + cq_measure(q);`
;
;
; RUN: env CQ_DEADARG_DBG=1 %cq-opt -load-pass-plugin %cq-pass -passes=cq-lowering -S %s > %t.cqd0.ll 2> %t.err
; RUN: %filecheck %s < %t.cqd0.ll
; RUN: %filecheck %s --check-prefix=NODROP --allow-empty < %t.err
;
; The ordered call sequence of @main (derived from the lowered module; SSA names
; wildcarded, constants — every dropped `0` and every angle — kept):
; Between consecutive matches NO other runtime/clone call may appear, so the
; runtime stream is pinned EXACTLY, not as a subsequence.
; CHECK-LABEL: define {{.*}}@main(
; CHECK-NOT: call {{.*}}@{{(cqrt_|cq_template_|__cq_q_)}}
; CHECK: call i32 @atoi(ptr nocapture noundef %{{[a-zA-Z0-9_.]+}})
; CHECK-NOT: call {{.*}}@{{(cqrt_|cq_template_|__cq_q_)}}
; CHECK: call i32 @cqrt_alloc_i32(i32 %{{[a-zA-Z0-9_.]+}})
; CHECK-NOT: call {{.*}}@{{(cqrt_|cq_template_|__cq_q_)}}
; CHECK: call void @cqrt_ry_i32(i32 %{{[a-zA-Z0-9_.]+}}, double 5.000000e-01)
; CHECK-NOT: call {{.*}}@{{(cqrt_|cq_template_|__cq_q_)}}
; CHECK: call i32 @cq_template_mul_i32_hl(i32 %{{[a-zA-Z0-9_.]+}}, i32 3)
; CHECK-NOT: call {{.*}}@{{(cqrt_|cq_template_|__cq_q_)}}
; CHECK: call i32 @__cq_q_h_01(i32 noundef 0, i32 noundef %{{[a-zA-Z0-9_.]+}})
; CHECK-NOT: call {{.*}}@{{(cqrt_|cq_template_|__cq_q_)}}
; CHECK: call i32 @cq_template_xor_i32(i32 %{{[a-zA-Z0-9_.]+}}, i32 %{{[a-zA-Z0-9_.]+}})
; CHECK-NOT: call {{.*}}@{{(cqrt_|cq_template_|__cq_q_)}}
; CHECK: call i32 @cq_template_icmp_eq_i32_hl(i32 %{{[a-zA-Z0-9_.]+}}, i32 10)
; CHECK-NOT: call {{.*}}@{{(cqrt_|cq_template_|__cq_q_)}}
; CHECK: call void @cqrt_rz_i1(i32 %{{[a-zA-Z0-9_.]+}}, double 3.141590e+00), !cq.branchphase !10
; CHECK-NOT: call {{.*}}@{{(cqrt_|cq_template_|__cq_q_)}}
; CHECK: call void @cq_template_icmp_eq_i32_hl_unc(i32 %{{[a-zA-Z0-9_.]+}}, i32 %{{[a-zA-Z0-9_.]+}}, i32 10)
; CHECK-NOT: call {{.*}}@{{(cqrt_|cq_template_|__cq_q_)}}
